================================================================================
  MatcoreDSL Fused Epilogue vs PyTorch Unfused Kernels (FP16)
  Activation: sigmoid(tanh(gelu(relu(A @ B))))
  PyTorch uses 5 separate kernel launches (cuBLAS + 4 elementwise)
  MatcoreDSL fuses everything into minimal kernel launches
================================================================================

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Size: 1024×1024  (FP16, 0.002 TFLOP matmul)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PyTorch (5 kernels):     0.15 ms  ( 14.8 TFLOPS)
  MatcoreDSL (fused):      0.29 ms  (  7.3 TFLOPS)
  Speedup:              0.50x ⚠️  PyTorch

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Size: 2048×2048  (FP16, 0.017 TFLOP matmul)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PyTorch (5 kernels):     0.87 ms  ( 19.7 TFLOPS)
  MatcoreDSL (fused):      0.85 ms  ( 20.3 TFLOPS)
  Speedup:              1.03x 🏆 MatcoreDSL

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Size: 4096×4096  (FP16, 0.137 TFLOP matmul)
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  PyTorch (5 kernels):     7.74 ms  ( 17.8 TFLOPS)
  MatcoreDSL (fused):      4.73 ms  ( 29.0 TFLOPS)
  Speedup:              1.64x 🏆 MatcoreDSL

================================================================================
  NOTE: PyTorch pays 4 extra GMEM round-trips (read+write each op).
  MatcoreDSL fuses the entire epilogue chain into the matmul output path.
================================================================================
